The references the book leans on most
This book draws on a few hundred papers, datasets, and tools. The map below shows how they connect to the chapters that cite them. Each chapter sits on the outer ring, grouped by part. Each dot is a reference. A reference cited by one chapter sits near it; one cited across several chapters is pulled toward the middle. The papers near the center are the ones the whole book leans on.
Hover over a dot to see the reference, and click it to open the paper. Hover over a chapter to see everything it cites, and click it to go to that chapter.
{
  const top = data.refs.filter((r) =&gt; r.chapters.length &gt;= 4)
    .sort((a, b) =&gt; b.chapters.length - a.chapters.length || (b.year ?? 0) - (a.year ?? 0));
  return html`&lt;table class="table table-sm refmap-table"&gt;
    &lt;thead&gt;&lt;tr&gt;&lt;th&gt;Reference&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th class="refmap-n"&gt;Chapters&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Cited in&lt;/th&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/thead&gt;
    &lt;tbody&gt;${top.map((r) =&gt; html`&lt;tr&gt;
      &lt;td&gt;&lt;a href="${refUrl(r)}" target="_blank" rel="noopener"&gt;${r.title}&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span class="refmap-muted"&gt;${r.authors}${r.year ? `, ${r.year}` : ""}&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;td class="refmap-n"&gt;${r.chapters.length}&lt;/td&gt;
      &lt;td&gt;${r.chapters.map((c, i) =&gt; html`${i ? ", " : ""}&lt;a href="${chapterById.get(c).href}"&gt;${chapterById.get(c).short}&lt;/a&gt;`)}&lt;/td&gt;
    &lt;/tr&gt;`)}&lt;/tbody&gt;
  &lt;/table&gt;`;
}
